{number: 156}
{title: Fill My Cup, Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Like the woman at the well I was [G7] seeking
For things that could not satis-[C] fy;
And then I heard my Savior [F] speaking:
“Draw from My [C] well that [G7] never shall run [C] dry.”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Fill my [C] cup, Lord, I lift it [G7] up, Lord!
Come and quench this thirsting of my [C] soul;
Bread of [C] heaven, feed me till I [F] want no more,
Fill my [C] cup, fill it [G7] up and make me [C] whole!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There [C] are millions in this world who are [G7] craving
The pleasure earthly things af-[C] ford;
But none can match the wondrous [F] treasure
That I [C] find in [G7] Jesus Christ my [C] Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
So, [C] my brother, if the things this world [G7] gave you
Leave hungers that won't pass a-[C] way,
My blessed Lord will come and [F] save you,
If you [C] kneel to [G7] Him and humbly [C] pray.
{end_of_verse}
